  "applies": true,
  "fixmes": [],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`src/evidence.rs#fn[validate_evidence_file]` has a parameter named `errors`, so it is a site of `requirements.ci.errors`.\n\n**Violation matches.** There are four `return` matches. All of them are on parse or decoding failures of the one evidence file, and `requirements.ci.errors` explicitly allows those to be a single failed check.\n- Read failure: the function pushes `cannot read evidence` and returns.\n- JSON failure: the function pushes `invalid JSON` and returns.\n- Evidence-format failure: `evidence_format::view` fails and the function pushes `invalid evidence format`.\n- Non-object: the function pushes `expected a JSON object`.\n\nEvery later check reads fields from the parsed object, so each one depends on the contents that failed to parse. A return there does not skip an independent check. Each return pushes exactly one error. `crate::evidence_format::check_native` runs on the native value before the object check, so it is not skipped by that return.\n\n**Well-formed records.** After parsing, the function does not return early. It runs these checks in turn, and each pushes its own error:\n- `check_keys`\n- the `references` digest check\n- the requirement text checks (empty text, and text that changed from the expected text)\n- the `determination` check\n- the `rationale` check\n- the false-determination report\n- `validate_dependencies` for orphaned records\n- `validate_input` for every element of `inputs`\n\nA failure in one field does not stop the others. The helpers `string_field` and `array_field` return `None` after recording an error, and the caller uses `if let` so the other checks still run.\n\n**Duplicates.** Each condition is reported once. `string_field` and `array_field` report a missing or mistyped field once. `check_native` leaves the application-level field diagnostics to the individual validators and reports only freshness findings those validators cannot explain. The false-determination message is a separate condition from the rationale-empty message.\n\nThe site meets the continue-after-failure, report-every-failure and no-duplicate obligations.",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "file": "src/evidence.rs",
      "item": "fn[validate_evidence_file]",
      "hash": "a5b094bae2358675e9aecc733eb4ce8ebfd79a3a8a8af530eb394135b3aa8823"
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.ci.errors",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.ci.errors"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::::{req} errors",
        "Repository validation MUST continue after a failed check and report every failed",
        "check it finds in one run, each as a {term}`requirements.ci.validation_error`.",
        "This is a convention for every validation error; the requirement for each check",
        "states which conditions that check reports. A file that cannot be parsed, such as",
        "a malformed `habeas.toml`, `book.toml`, or evidence file, is one failed check:",
        "its error MAY report only the first parse or decoding problem in that file, and",
        "checks that do not depend on its contents MUST still run.",
        "",
        "The code that sequences the repository's checks carries out the first paragraph.",
        "A repository-validation function that collects validation errors MUST hold them",
        "in a parameter or local variable named `errors`, and a function with such a",
        "variable is a site below; authoring code that collects errors only to abort is",
        "not one. After one of its checks fails, a site MUST still run every later check",
        "that does not depend on the failed check's result, including later checks in the",
        "same loop iteration, and MUST NOT report one failure twice.",
        "",
        "::::{sites} error_accumulators",
        "```yaml",
        "language: rust",
        "paths: [src, crates/habeas-sdk/src]",
        "exclude: [src/authoring/inputs.rs, src/authoring/tools.rs]",
        "rule:",
        "  kind: function_item",
        "  has:",
        "    stopBy: { kind: function_item }",
        "    any:",
        "      - kind: parameter",
        "        has: { field: pattern, regex: \"^errors$\" }",
        "      - kind: let_declaration",
        "        has: { field: pattern, regex: \"^errors$\" }",
        "  not:",
        "    inside:",
        "      stopBy: end",
        "      kind: mod_item",
        "      has: { field: name, regex: \"^tests$\" }",
        "match:",
        "  - \"fn check(value: &str, errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\"",
        "  - |",
        "    fn run() {",
        "        let mut errors: BTreeSet<String> = BTreeSet::new();",
        "        check(\"\", &mut errors);",
        "    }",
        "no_match:",
        "  - \"fn check(value: &str, discovery_errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\"",
        "  - |",
        "    fn run() {",
        "        let mut problems = Vec::new();",
        "        check(\"\", &mut problems);",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    mod tests {",
        "        fn check(errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}",
        "    }",
        "```",
        "::::",
        "",
        "::::{violations} early_exits",
        "```yaml",
        "language: rust",
        "paths: [src, crates/habeas-sdk/src]",
        "within: error_accumulators",
        "rule:",
        "  any:",
        "    - kind: try_expression",
        "    - kind: return_expression",
        "    - kind: continue_expression",
        "    - kind: break_expression",
        "match:",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(v: &Value, errors: &mut Vec<String>) -> Option<u8> {",
        "        let n = v.as_u64()?;",
        "        if v.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "        Some(n as u8)",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(items: &[Value], errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        for item in items {",
        "            if !item.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); continue; }",
        "            if item.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "        }",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(v: &Value, errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        if !v.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); return; }",
        "        if v.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(items: &[Value], errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        for item in items {",
        "            if !item.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); break; }",
        "        }",
        "        if items.is_empty() { errors.push(\"empty\".into()); }",
        "    }",
        "no_match:",
        "  - |",
        "    fn parse(v: &Value) -> Option<u8> {",
        "        let n = v.as_u64()?;",
        "        Some(n as u8)",
        "    }",
        "```",
        "::::",
        ":::::"
      ]
    },
